# Reconstruction data: photographs, point clouds, meshes and run outputs are
# large and are never committed. Everything under data/ is either your capture
# set or reproducible from it plus a config, which is the point of the
# run-directory layout.
#
# Note: COLMAP feature databases and fused point clouds routinely exceed
# GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit (data/runs/sample/database.db is 154 MB),
# so tracking run outputs would break `git push` anyway.
#
# Because the photographs are NOT in git, keep a backup of data/raw/ somewhere
# else -- they are the one input that cannot be regenerated.
data/

# Colab hand-off bundles
*.zip

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Word lock/temp files (created while a .docx is open)
~$*
